---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Falck | Review Ready"
  description="Falck turns non-technical work into review-ready branches with summaries engineers can trust."
  theme="light"
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden pt-24 pb-20">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 backdrop-grid opacity-60"></div>
      <div class="absolute -top-20 left-[12%] h-[340px] w-[340px] rounded-full bg-emerald-300/40 blur-[140px] glow-pulse"></div>
      <div class="absolute bottom-[-25%] right-[6%] h-[420px] w-[420px] rounded-full bg-sky-300/40 blur-[160px] float-soft"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6 reveal">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-white/70 px-4 py-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-600 border border-white/80">
          Review-ready handoff
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-slate-950">
          The handoff is a real branch with a real summary. No more "please imagine this."
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600">
          Falck keeps the intent attached to the work so engineers do not have to reverse-engineer your vision from a
          screenshot. The PR reads like a calm human wrote it because you did, with a little help.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
          <Button href="/download">Download Falck</Button>
          <Button href="/features" variant="secondary">Back to the story</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] items-center">
      <div class="space-y-4 reveal">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-emerald-500">Clear summary</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Falck writes the story with you.</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600">
          Notes become a clean summary and a list of changes. Reviewers see what changed and why, without a meeting.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Branch name stays tidy and readable
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Summary reads like a human (because it is)
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Engineers can merge or keep building on the same branch
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="app-window reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="app-window-bar">
          <span>Falck Desktop</span>
          <span>Save Changes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-400">
            <span>Save queue</span>
            <span class="text-emerald-500">Ready</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid gap-3">
            <div class="surface-muted px-4 py-3 text-sm">
              <p class="font-semibold">Summary</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">"Refined onboarding copy, updated CTA, fixed FAQ order"</p>
            </div>
            <div class="surface-muted px-4 py-3 text-sm">
              <p class="font-semibold">Highlights</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">3 files changed, ready for review</p>
            </div>
            <div class="surface-dark px-4 py-3 text-sm">
              <p class="font-semibold">Create update</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-emerald-100/70">PR ready in one click</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100/80 bg-emerald-50 px-4 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-700">
            "I made a change" now comes with a diff. You're welcome.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="surface p-6 reveal">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-emerald-500">Respect</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Reviewers stay happy</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
          Engineers get a clean diff with context, not a mystery batch of edits.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="surface p-6 reveal-delay-1">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-slate-500">Continuity</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Same branch, same intent</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
          The technical team can keep building on the branch, so your work is the starting point, not a detour.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="surface p-6 reveal-delay-2">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-slate-500">Speed</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Less meeting, more shipping</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
          The intent is clear, the review is easy, and your team gets to ship sooner.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto px-6 pb-28">
    <div class="surface p-10 md:p-12 text-center reveal">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-400">Go from idea to merge</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Make the handoff feel easy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Falck keeps your intent attached to the work so the team can review, polish, or ship without rework.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <Button href="/features/team-mode">Explore Team Mode</Button>
        <Button href="/features/local-studio" variant="secondary">Local Studio mode</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
